@@@!atrep

@@/ at-markdown: the standard-library Markdown dialektos,
@@/ realizing the dialektos the spec's inheritance examples treat
@@/ as hypothetical. Sim symbols mirror Markdown markers. The
@@/ structure is flat, Markdown-style: headings do not nest
@@/ content, and list items form flat sibling runs without
@@/ containers. Inline code and code blocks use the core enlexis
@@/ forms; images use the core enmedia form.
@@/
@@/ Everything is inherited from at-html, the HTML syntax mapper:
@@/ the shared element semantics come in via full inheritance
@@/ (excluding the list containers, span, and division - markdown
@@/ is flat), and emphasis and strong are imported under the
@@/ markdown markers * and **. The Markdown exomorphosis is this
@@/ dialektos's own; its HTML rendering is entirely inherited
@@/ from at-html.html.exo through the lineage (spec: Rule
@@/ Resolution and Inheritance).

@@::at-html:-:[-- .. , _ / ! ~]

@@::at-html::/ *

@@::at-html::! **
